@startuml 07-interfaces
' =====================================================================
' Key interfaces and extension points
' Traces to: FR-23, FR-24, FR-37..FR-40, NFR-3, NFR-4, NFR-11
'
' Changes in this revision:
'   Rerun is PER SUBMISSION, so ILearningPlatform needs to locate an
'   individual submission before clicking its rerun button. It no
'   longer pulls submission files at all: the autograder script
'   already has them.
'
'   No claim step. Rerun is per submission, so one container works on
'   a submission at a time and there is nothing to race against.
'
'   AiNeedMarker is new: it applies the instructor's per-target
'   ai_feedback_policy to the functional test outcomes to decide which
'   targets need AI feedback at all.
'
'   + IGradingClient: the boundary the autograder container talks to.
'     It runs on Gradescope infrastructure, so this is the only surface
'     it gets, and it is how credentials stay on our side (OQ-11).
' =====================================================================

title Key Interfaces and Extension Points

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
' Platform abstraction -- Student C
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
package "Platform Integration (Student C)" #FBE6D4 {

  interface ILearningPlatform <<abstract>> {
    +authenticate() : None
    +find_submission(platform_assignment_id,\n platform_submission_id) : SubmissionLocator
    +trigger_rerun(locator) : RerunResult
  }

  class GradescopePlatform {
    -page : playwright.Page
    -selectors : SelectorMap
    --
    +authenticate()
    +find_submission(...)
    +trigger_rerun(...)
  }

  class FakePlatform {
    Records rerun calls. Lets the
    nightly trigger be tested with
    no browser and no account.
  }

  class SelectorMap {
    +login_email : str
    +login_password : str
    +assignment_rows : str
    +manage_submissions_link : str
    +submission_rows : str
    +submission_id_attr : str
    +rerun_autograder_button : str
    +rerun_confirm_button : str
    --
    Every CSS selector in one file.
    When Gradescope reskins, this is
    the only thing that changes.
  }

  class NightlyTrigger {
    -platform : ILearningPlatform
    -client : IGradingClient
    --
    +run() : TriggerRunSummary
    --
    Thin on purpose. Asks the service
    which submissions still have
    PENDING tasks, then clicks rerun on
    each. Never calls an LLM.
  }

  class AutograderEntrypoint {
    -client : IGradingClient
    -runner : ITestRunner
    -marker : AiNeedMarker
    -grader : AIGradingComponent
    --
    +main() : int
    --
    Ships inside the platform
    autograder zip. Decides from
    grading_mode whether to invoke
    the AI component now.
  }

  class AiNeedMarker {
    +mark(targets, outcomes) : AiMark[]
    --
    Applies each target's
    ai_feedback_policy to its test
    outcomes. The AUTOGRADER policy
    delegates to instructor-supplied
    logic. Pure function of its
    inputs, so it is the easiest
    thing in the system to test.
  }

  AutograderEntrypoint --> AiNeedMarker

  interface ITestRunner <<abstract>> {
    +run(targets, submission_dir) : TestOutcome[]
  }

  class JUnitRunner
  class PytestRunner

  ILearningPlatform <|.. GradescopePlatform
  ILearningPlatform <|.. FakePlatform
  GradescopePlatform --> SelectorMap
  NightlyTrigger ..> ILearningPlatform
  ITestRunner <|.. JUnitRunner
  ITestRunner <|.. PytestRunner
  AutograderEntrypoint ..> ITestRunner
}

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
' AI grading -- Student A. Runs INSIDE the autograder container.
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
package "AI Grading (Student A)" #D6E4F0 {

  class AIGradingComponent {
    -providers : ILLMProvider[]
    -builder : PromptBuilder
    -comparator : ResponseComparator
    -estimator : ConfidenceEstimator
    -client : IGradingClient
    --
    +grade(task_id) : FeedbackItem
    --
    Same code in both modes. The only
    difference is who calls it.
  }

  interface ILLMProvider <<abstract>> {
    +name : str
    +model : str
    +generate_feedback(req : FeedbackRequest) : FeedbackResponse
    +estimated_cost(req) : float
  }

  class ClaudeProvider
  class OpenAIProvider
  class GeminiProvider
  class FakeProvider {
    Deterministic canned responses.
    Required so the test suite runs
    in CI with no API key and no bill.
  }

  class PromptBuilder {
    +build(rubric, guidance,\n outcomes, files) : str
    +version : str
  }

  class ResponseComparator {
    +compare(responses) : Comparison
    +select(responses) : FeedbackResponse
  }

  class ConfidenceEstimator {
    +estimate(responses) : float
  }

  ILLMProvider <|.. ClaudeProvider
  ILLMProvider <|.. OpenAIProvider
  ILLMProvider <|.. GeminiProvider
  ILLMProvider <|.. FakeProvider

  AIGradingComponent o--> "1..*" ILLMProvider
  AIGradingComponent --> PromptBuilder
  AIGradingComponent --> ResponseComparator
  AIGradingComponent --> ConfidenceEstimator
}

AutograderEntrypoint --> AIGradingComponent

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
' The container's only window onto our data -- Student B
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
package "Service Boundary (Student B)" #DCEFD9 {

  interface IGradingClient <<abstract>> {
    +get_config(platform_assignment_id) : AssignmentConfig
    +post_submission(ref, outcomes, files) : SubmissionResult
    +get_submission_state(platform_submission_id) : SubmissionState
    +get_pending_tasks(submission_id) : GradingTaskRef[]
    +get_feedback_request(task_id) : FeedbackRequest
    +post_feedback(task_id, result) : None
    +mark_ai_complete(submission_id) : bool
    +get_selected_feedback(submission_id) : FeedbackPackage
    +list_submissions_pending_ai(mode) : SubmissionLocator[]
  }

  class HttpGradingClient {
    -base_url : str
    -assignment_token : str
    --
    Per-assignment bearer token,
    scoped to one assignment's rows.
    Never a DB credential.
  }

  class FakeGradingClient {
    In-memory. Lets the whole
    autograder script be tested
    offline.
  }

  interface IGradingRepository <<abstract>> {
    +get_assignment_config(...) : AssignmentConfig
    +upsert_submission(ref) : str
    +record_outcomes(...) : None
    +create_pending_tasks(...) : GradingTaskRef[]
    +create_tasks(submission_id, marks) : GradingTaskRef[]
    +build_feedback_request(task_id) : FeedbackRequest
    +save_feedback(task_id, result) : None
    +mark_ai_complete_if_all_done(submission_id) : bool
    +get_selected_feedback(...) : FeedbackPackage
    +list_submissions_pending_ai(mode) : SubmissionLocator[]
  }

  class SqlGradingRepository
  class InMemoryRepository

  IGradingClient <|.. HttpGradingClient
  IGradingClient <|.. FakeGradingClient
  IGradingRepository <|.. SqlGradingRepository
  IGradingRepository <|.. InMemoryRepository
}

AIGradingComponent ..> IGradingClient
AutograderEntrypoint ..> IGradingClient
NightlyTrigger ..> IGradingClient

note as N1 #FFF8DC
  **Why IGradingClient and IGradingRepository
  are separate interfaces.**
  The repository is in-process SQL on our cloud
  host. The client is HTTPS from someone else's
  container. Collapsing them would mean shipping
  database credentials inside the autograder
  zip, which is OQ-11 option (a).

  The Web API implements the client surface on
  top of the repository. Keeping the two
  interfaces distinct is what makes the
  credential boundary visible in code rather
  than a deployment convention nobody remembers.
end note

note as N2 #FFF8DC
  **Every interface ships with a fake.**
  FakePlatform, FakeProvider, FakeGradingClient
  and InMemoryRepository are not extras. They
  are what lets four people work in parallel in
  week two rather than week six, and what makes
  TR-2 and TR-8 achievable with no Gradescope
  account and no API bill.

  Rule: adding an abstract method means adding
  it to the fake in the same commit.
end note

note as N3 #FFF8DC
  **mark_ai_complete is conditional on purpose.**
  It sets ai_graded_submitted_at only when no
  task is still NEEDED, and returns whether it
  did. Setting it unconditionally would strand
  failed targets permanently ungraded, because
  the guard short-circuits before the task query
  ever runs.
end note

note as N4 #FFF8DC
  **ITestRunner exists so the system is not
  Java-only.** The SRS names JUnit, but a
  generic autograder for CS courses will meet
  pytest and others. Same shape as
  ILearningPlatform: one interface, one
  implementation to start.
end note

@enduml
